  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{励|はげ}ます: to encourage someone\n- {励|はげ}まし⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{言葉|ことば}→言葉：02880_kotoba⟧: words of encouragement\n- ⟦{互|たが}いに→互いに：07150_tagaini⟧{励|はげ}まし⟦{合|あ}う→合う：10466_au⟧: to encourage each other\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{励|はげ}ましている describes the ongoing act of encouraging someone.\n\nPASSIVE:\n{励|はげ}まされる (to be encouraged) is very common — often more natural than the active form in Japanese.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{励|はげ}み→励み：07282_hagemi⟧: encouragement, incentive (noun)\n- ⟦{励|はげ}む→励む：11822_hagemu⟧: to strive, to work hard (different verb — intransitive)\n- ⟦{応援|おうえん}→応援：01900_ouen⟧⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to cheer on, to support (broader)\n- ⟦{元気|げんき}づける→元気づける：21545_genkizukeru⟧: to cheer up (more casual)\n\nUSAGE:\n{励|はげ}ます implies emotional support directed at someone who is struggling or discouraged.",
